  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I've been wondering why turning up the gain on a VRCSpatialAudioSource in a world didn't seem to be doing anything, when the documentation page says that there's only a limit for avatars, of 10db:  https://creators.vrchat.com/worlds/components/vrc_spatialaudiosource/\n\nHowever, after googling around some more, I found an old Medium article that says there's a limit for worlds too, of 24db:  https://medium.com/vrchat/vrchat-the-sound-of-progress-3c4ab4fb5472\n\nIf that's accurate, please put it in the actual documentation!  (In fact, maybe have the component automatically set its gain value back down to the limit when a world creator tries to set it higher in the inspector?)",
